{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding","id":1122651,"title":"Obfuscate and other Supernatural hiding","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-07-30T01:57:27-07:00","id":1122651,"title":"Obfuscate and other Supernatural hiding","content":"What do you think would pierce obfuscate? What are some other hiding skills and what do you think would pierce those?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12894-grasharm","name":"Grasharm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12894_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"22"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T02:35:18-07:00","id":1122657,"title":"","content":"Mind sphere, as obfuscate tricks people's minds into not being seen as opposed to physically cloaking them with the naked eye as one would do with forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T03:00:24-07:00","id":1122660,"title":"","content":"Yup. Mind would do it pretty easily. Either that or Spirit sense for the Garou or Matter/Life sense for the Vampires.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T04:24:39-07:00","id":1122664,"title":"","content":"SInce auspex allows you to engage in dealing with obfuscate even at its lowest levels I'd argue anything that enhances the senses would have similar options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T07:58:03-07:00","id":1122704,"title":"","content":"A Mind 1 effect to shield your mind from outside influence should do the trick. It would also help against other mind affecting powers vampires have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12710-pazuzuaxelf","name":"PazuzuAxelf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T08:19:18-07:00","id":1122709,"title":"","content":"Would a Correspondence sight (or sense) Effect detect a Kindred using Obfuscate?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-30T08:23:01-07:00","id":1122710,"title":"","content":"Correspondance/mater 1 could do it, sensing that something is in front of you but invisible, it's not really piercing trough obfuscate but you could be aware that something is wrong","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T00:00:53-07:00","id":1122929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1122710#post1122710\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Correspondance/mater 1 could do it, sensing that something is in front of you but invisible, it's not really piercing trough obfuscate but you could be aware that something is wrong</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> But that's not how Obfuscate works. It tricks the person into not seeing things. By finding Flaws in the trick the whole thing ends up colapsing thus &quot;piecing&quot; obfuscate. OF course just because someone with Corr one COULD break obfuscate doesn't mean they should. It should be a matter of successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T07:13:36-07:00","id":1123008,"title":"","content":"Yeah but if you're tricked into thinking there is nothing in front of you, and yours sphere senses tell you otherwise, that a pretty big flaw in the obfuscate","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12946-emerick","name":"Emerick","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12946_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"156"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T20:06:08-07:00","id":1123284,"title":"","content":"I'm thinking that Prime 1 would be useful in sensing the quintessence present in Obfuscated vampires' blood pools, though the mage using it might not realize that it's a vampire she's sensing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T21:45:11-07:00","id":1123308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Emerick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123008#post1123008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah but if you're tricked into thinking there is nothing in front of you, and yours sphere senses tell you otherwise, that a pretty big flaw in the obfuscate</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That is a pretty big flaw.. since that's how Auspex breaks Obfuscate. You find enough &quot;flaws' that you see through it. That's how I'd run it for a mage trying to pull the same thing. This doesn't mean &quot;every mage beats obfuscate all the time&quot; anymore than everyone with Auspex 1 sees through everything forever. I&quot;d run it as a straight contested action, with the Vampire probably winning since the mage isn't going to have the time to build up successes. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-07-31T22:46:14-07:00","id":1123321,"title":"","content":"I think it highly depends on what game you want to run.<br /> <br /> in a pure Mage game where vampires play a lesser role, I agree with the above posts - there are many, easy ways to pierce Obfuscate. Heck, almost any sphere can do it:<br /> <br /> <b>Life+Matter</b> - Sense the pattern of dead flesh of the Vampire hidden from sight<br /> <b>Forces</b> - Sense the motions of the air pushed away by the invisible vampire, sense its motions, sense the subtle, tiny things it moves from its mere steps.<br /> <b>Correspondence</b> - Sense the lack of empty space where the vampire is, sense the changes in space.<br /> <b>Mind</b> - Resist the actual Mind effect of Obfuscate<br /> <b>Spirit</b> - Sense the Aura of the Obfuscated vampire.<br /> <b>Prime</b> - Sense the quintessence pattern where none visually should be.<br /> <b>Entropy</b> - Entropy *might* be able to do it as well, if you rule that it can sense the absolute entropic stasis that is inherent in Vampires<br /> <br /> One could argue that in the Vampire game, Auspex actually uses the Spirit and Forces combination to break through Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> <br /> Now, wether all that is actually as utterly easy as it sounds here depends on the game the ST wants to run.<br /> If they want to make things harder (or simply more atmospheric) and require more roll successes, they could rule that the mind-bending abilities of Obfuscate actually try to hide the *results* of the sphere's Magicks detecting the anomalies from the Mage's mind;<br /> This is not the ability to influence True Magick itself - not at all - but Obfuscate simply making the Mage's mind ignorant of what the Magick is telling them. Which is essentially how Obfuscate works in the first place - the mind becomes oblivious to the obvious.<br /> <br /> And then, of course, there are the various attempts of crossover-rules by the hard numbers, requiring sphere level at X to piece Obfuscate at X. I'm not a fan of that, at all. I loathe it, as those rules bluntly compare sphere levels to discipline levels because of the sole reason of '<i>same numbers'</i>, without any regard of what those numbers actually mean in the different gamelines, and their difference in potency.<br /> <br /> Personally, and in order to make things more exciting than <i>'I use sphere X's first level with a single success and notice something is wrong'</i>, I would rule that the Mage needs to roll successes equal or more to 2x the Obfuscate user's discipline level. This makes the whole process independant of the silly 'Sphere level vs. Obfuscate level' rule, while still giving more potent Obfuscate using NPCs (or players) an edge. Many mages won't go 'I churn out a 10-success sensory effect' at the start of their day or scene.<br /> And if that is not balancing enough, in case of a full Players vs Players Con one-shot crossover or the like, the Mind sphere could be *required* in the mix to see through Obfuscate's mind influence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-01-2017, 01:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T00:27:50-07:00","id":1123344,"title":"","content":"I am not saying it should be I get one success with any sphere and &quot;Hah all mages casually see through obfuscate&quot; I think they potentially can given enough time. Generally how i would run this is the Vampire Rolls Manipulation+STealth/subterfuge where as the mage can only roll arete. This gives generally the advantage to the Vampire if they want to sneak past a mage or vanish infront of him. <br /> <br /> On the otherhand the Mage who wants to go out vampire hunting and spends time on a serious ritual of pericing obfuscate has her options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T01:07:23-07:00","id":1123353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123344#post1123344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am not saying it should be I get one success with any sphere</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, my post wasn't in response to you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was a general thread-topic thing.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> That said, my usual issue with Arete vs skillpool contested rolls is that you then require high-Arete Archmages to be able to contest even potential fresh-out-of-chargen splats that specialize in those skills. It's relatively easy to justify an 8-dice attribute+ability combo with even a potential specialization out of CG if it's a character's thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 08-01-2017, 04:10 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T01:27:18-07:00","id":1123358,"title":"","content":"Quick to fix: double the Arete successes when comparing with the results of a regular roll.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T01:27:46-07:00","id":1123359,"title":"","content":"Sorry, using something like Forces 1 to detect the small shifts in the room... Obfuscate 1 is *telling you that there isn't anything going on*.<br /> <br /> A human thinks someone is in the room, and takes pictures. They check the pictures. They see nothing (for now), as Obfuscate is *telling them they are alone*. Same applies to someone watching a video if they are in range. The Spheres are just another source of info, and one that you will ignore because of Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Mind can break Obfuscate, certainly. The other Spheres? Well Spirit means one of your spiritual allies could tell you, since Obfuscate only works on &quot;minds&quot;, not ghosts and spirits. Correspondance, Matter, Entropy, Forces, yes there are problems in the room, small things aren't right (Correspondance might be saying &quot;hmm these two objects look closer together than they are, I think my senses are being warped&quot;) but Obfuscate IS you ignoring that. I mean for crying out loud your EYES and all your other senses are screaming &quot;VAMPIRE&quot; as loud as they can and your brain is ignoring it because Obfuscate is fundamentally not about the senses in its basic concept.<br /> <br /> Personally if a Mage character had no Mind, and had Awareness, I'd let them roll to get a &quot;chill up their spine&quot; or something similar so that they can teleport away or something and not get melted by the blood-vomit of the Assamite who just snuck up behind them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-01-2017, 04:30 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T03:27:49-07:00","id":1123383,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123359#post1123359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorry, using something like Forces 1 to detect the small shifts in the room... Obfuscate 1 is *telling you that there isn't anything going on*.<br /> <br /> A human thinks someone is in the room, and takes pictures. They check the pictures. They see nothing (for now), as Obfuscate is *telling them they are alone*. Same applies to someone watching a video if they are in range. The Spheres are just another source of info, and one that you will ignore because of Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Mind can break Obfuscate, certainly. The other Spheres? Well Spirit means one of your spiritual allies could tell you, since Obfuscate only works on &quot;minds&quot;, not ghosts and spirits. Correspondance, Matter, Entropy, Forces, yes there are problems in the room, small things aren't right (Correspondance might be saying &quot;hmm these two objects look closer together than they are, I think my senses are being warped&quot;) but Obfuscate IS you ignoring that. I mean for crying out loud your EYES and all your other senses are screaming &quot;VAMPIRE&quot; as loud as they can and your brain is ignoring it because Obfuscate is fundamentally not about the senses in its basic concept.<br /> <br /> Personally if a Mage character had no Mind, and had Awareness, I'd let them roll to get a &quot;chill up their spine&quot; or something similar so that they can teleport away or something and not get melted by the blood-vomit of the Assamite who just snuck up behind them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate, at least below elder levels, is telling the mind <i>not to see</i> the vampire. It doesn't prevent detections using other senses. In fact, it says:<br /> &quot;Since the vampire fully retains his physical substance, he must be careful to avoid contact with anything that may disclose his presence (knocking over a vase, bumping into someone). Even a whispered word or the scuffing of a shoe against the floor can be enough to disrupt the power.&quot;<br /> <br /> So electromagnetic sense, echolocation, mystic spirit-awareness etc. should be quite disruptive for Obfuscate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T03:48:55-07:00","id":1123388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123383#post1123383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Obfuscate, at least below elder levels, is telling the mind <i>not to see</i> the vampire. It doesn't prevent detections using other senses. In fact, it says:<br /> &quot;Since the vampire fully retains his physical substance, he must be careful to avoid contact with anything that may disclose his presence (knocking over a vase, bumping into someone). Even a whispered word or the scuffing of a shoe against the floor can be enough to disrupt the power.&quot;<br /> <br /> So electromagnetic sense, echolocation, mystic spirit-awareness etc. should be quite disruptive for Obfuscate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate can be disrupted by making loud noises or disrupting other objects, yes. Speaking, wading through water, stepping on a creaky board...<br /> <br /> But the reason this breaks Obfuscate is that it removes the pretense that there is nothing in the room. When a board creaks the &quot;I'm not here&quot;-ness of Obfuscate becomes difficult to maintain (so they have to roll to keep Obfuscate up). If someone *has good reason* to believe that they are not alone, then they can attempt to See the Unseen, but this is an active decision that someone actually has to make themselves, at which point practically any Sphere would do, yes. Realistically though, when a Mage hears a board creak, they don't whip out a Forces 1 effect to see if there is a weight sitting on the floor other than them, or use Spirit 1 to perceive local auras.<br /> <br /> So yes, Obfuscate does not edit the Vampire out of every sense available to those around them, but it does convince them that the Vampire isn't there. If they smell the Vampire's wet clothes, they don't immediately break Obfuscate. If they hear a floor creak, they don't immediately break Obfuscate. They rationalize those things away, not because of the power, but because of the way people just *behave* when they hear odd things. If you want to 100% override this mind control you need Mind, Mind 1 to reflexively detect that your mind is being controlled, and whatever level of Mind is needed to resist mind control would be needed too. Either that or the Vampire needs to mess up the Wits + Stealth roll when they step on the board.<br /> <br /> Now if a Mage randomly decides to construct a spacial map of the room they're in in their head using Correspondence, closing their eyes and building everything in their surroundings inside their mind... do they break Obfuscate by sensing the object moving around the room they're in? I think that's up for debate. On the one hand they're still getting the &quot;I'm not Here&quot; signal, and I think that would hold. On the other you could argue that Obfuscate edits Vampires out of mundane senses only, and if someone *happens* to do a detailed supernatural examination of their surroundings they will automatically break Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Note that this is all from a MTA perspective. If we go by VTM rules then it's a simple Perception + Awareness vs. Manipulation + Subterfuge, difficulty 7 for both. This rule is in there since the VTM book knows that comparing ratings and differently balanced powers won't always work and that it's easier to just go by rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11620,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","user":"twig","date":". 08-01-2017, 07:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T04:22:40-07:00","id":1123399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123388#post1123388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Obfuscate can be disrupted by making loud noises or disrupting other objects, yes. Speaking, wading through water, stepping on a creaky board...<br /> <br /> But the reason this breaks Obfuscate is that it removes the pretense that there is nothing in the room. When a board creaks the &quot;I'm not here&quot;-ness of Obfuscate becomes difficult to maintain (so they have to roll to keep Obfuscate up). If someone *has good reason* to believe that they are not alone, then they can attempt to See the Unseen, but this is an active decision that someone actually has to make themselves, at which point practically any Sphere would do, yes. Realistically though, when a Mage hears a board creak, they don't whip out a Forces 1 effect to see if there is a weight sitting on the floor other than them, or use Spirit 1 to perceive local auras.<br /> <br /> So yes, Obfuscate does not edit the Vampire out of every sense available to those around them, but it does convince them that the Vampire isn't there. If they smell the Vampire's wet clothes, they don't immediately break Obfuscate. If they hear a floor creak, they don't immediately break Obfuscate. They rationalize those things away, not because of the power, but because of the way people just *behave* when they hear odd things. If you want to 100% override this mind control you need Mind, Mind 1 to reflexively detect that your mind is being controlled, and whatever level of Mind is needed to resist mind control would be needed too. Either that or the Vampire needs to mess up the Wits + Stealth roll when they step on the board.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wait, you can Mind-defend <i>reflexively</i>? I thought you need to whip out the foci and do a counterspell.<br /> <br /> Anyway, when you have a feed showing that something significant is <i>there</i> while the vision feed is edited to say that there isn't, that's as imnothereness-breaking as a whisper or a knocked-over vase . . . actually <i>more</i> so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123388#post1123388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now if a Mage randomly decides to construct a spacial map of the room they're in in their head using Correspondence, closing their eyes and building everything in their surroundings inside their mind... do they break Obfuscate by sensing the object moving around the room they're in? I think that's up for debate. On the one hand they're still getting the &quot;I'm not Here&quot; signal, and I think that would hold. On the other you could argue that Obfuscate edits Vampires out of mundane senses only, and if someone *happens* to do a detailed supernatural examination of their surroundings they will automatically break Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> Note that this is all from a MTA perspective. If we go by VTM rules then it's a simple Perception + Awareness vs. Manipulation + Subterfuge, difficulty 7 for both. This rule is in there since the VTM book knows that comparing ratings and differently balanced powers won't always work and that it's easier to just go by rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obfuscate edits vampires out of being <i>visually</i> noticed; it keeps talking about preventing the vampire from being <i>seen</i>. Obfuscate 4+ will still keep fooling the visual perception (not the non-visual ones like distant-touch, spirit-feels and the like), but Obfuscate 2- explicitly breaks when the victim simply gets an alternate-sense impression that something <i>is</i> there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T04:33:09-07:00","id":1123402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123399#post1123399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait, you can Mind-defend <i>reflexively</i>? I thought you need to whip out the foci and do a counterspell.<br /> <br /> Anyway, when you have a feed showing that something significant is <i>there</i> while the vision feed is edited to say that there isn't, that's as imnothereness-breaking as a whisper or a knocked-over vase . . . actually <i>more</i> so.<br /> <br /> Obfuscate edits vampires out of being <i>visually</i> noticed; it keeps talking about preventing the vampire from being <i>seen</i>. Obfuscate 4+ will still keep fooling the visual perception (not the non-visual ones like distant-touch, spirit-feels and the like), but Obfuscate 2- explicitly breaks when the victim simply gets an alternate-sense impression that something <i>is</i> there.</div> </div> </div> </div>- Good point, forgot that Mages don't tend to get innate stuff... that said, a very potent Mage whose foci were mostly internal could fast-cast it without doing anything noticeable... but fast-casting isn't reflexive, it's just, well, fast.<br /> <br /> - Obfuscate 2 CAN break when these things happen, yes, but that's because extreme sensory feedback tests the limits of the illusion. This could be feedback to any of the senses. However Obfuscate 2 doesn't automatically break when these things happen, there is a roll to maintain it.<br /> <br /> 1: Vampire is in Obfuscate, Mage has no way of breaking this or knowing they're there (short of True Faith, Spiritual allies or some kind of ongoing effect that they'd need to have set up in the past).<br /> <br /> 2: Vampire makes scuffs his shoe and rolls to keep Obfuscate; the Mage hears it but rationalizes it away when they succeed in the roll to keep Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> 3: The Mage Player or NPC considers it for a moment and decides it's better to be safe than sorry. They perform a quick spell using a Sphere to try and detect the Vampire. At this point they are actively questioning the fact that the Vampire isn't there, and can qualify for Seeing the Unseen.<br /> <br /> 4: Either we're going fully by Mage and they find them b/c their effect overrides Obfuscate automatically, or we trust the Vampire writeup (which even mentions Magi) and we rolls Per+Aw vs. Man+Sub. I'd argue that if we're using a Vampire then using the VTM mechanics for Obfuscate is fair.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T04:51:33-07:00","id":1123404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123402#post1123402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> - Good point, forgot that Mages don't tend to get innate stuff... that said, a very potent Mage whose foci were mostly internal could fast-cast it without doing anything noticeable... but fast-casting isn't reflexive, it's just, well, fast.</div> </div> </div> </div>Amusiingly, fast-casting isn't even fast. In fact fast-casting and slow-casting can be done simultaneously. (Fast-casting just means casting something that isn't a mastered Rote.) But sure, you can forego the focus, yet that does not offer a way to make it reflexive as far as I know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123402#post1123402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">- Obfuscate 2 CAN break when these things happen, yes, but that's because extreme sensory feedback tests the limits of the illusion. This could be feedback to any of the senses. However Obfuscate 2 doesn't automatically break when these things happen, there is a roll to maintain it.<br /> <br /> 1: Vampire is in Obfuscate, Mage has no way of breaking this or knowing they're there (short of True Faith, Spiritual allies or some kind of ongoing effect that they'd need to have set up in the past).<br /> <br /> 2: Vampire makes scuffs his shoe and rolls to keep Obfuscate; the Mage hears it but rationalizes it away when they succeed in the roll to keep Obfuscate.<br /> <br /> 3: The Mage Player or NPC considers it for a moment and decides it's better to be safe than sorry. They perform a quick spell using a Sphere to try and detect the Vampire. At this point they are actively questioning the fact that the Vampire isn't there, and can qualify for Seeing the Unseen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, the normal rolls apply, yes. But I'd argue that &quot;I can sense a man-like figure on my echolocator/RADAR/space-sense/etc. but not by vision&quot; should call for a roll at best at difficulty 9 (&quot;walking through water&quot;), and more likely nastier than that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>11twiggins</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123402#post1123402\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4: Either we're going fully by Mage and they find them b/c their effect overrides Obfuscate automatically, or we trust the Vampire writeup (which even mentions Magi) and we rolls Per+Aw vs. Man+Sub. I'd argue that if we're using a Vampire then using the VTM mechanics for Obfuscate is fair.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, true, the consequences of lacking a unified framework on which all powers are built.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12622-vicky_molokh","name":"vicky_molokh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12622_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"75"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T05:01:13-07:00","id":1123406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>vicky_molokh</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123404#post1123404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, true, the consequences of lacking a unified framework on which all powers are built.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since I run VTM I just give everything powers that work in a VTM framework to be honest. Mages still have the Traditions and the Technocracy and &quot;Paradigms&quot;, but if you're playing Vampire the LAST thing you need is Paradox and Spheres and all that malarky. Werewolves keep stuff like Red Talons hating humans and Silver Fangs being uppity, but lose a lot of the mechanical stuff (Spirits as CCTV, Gifts).<br /> <br /> Like one of the Vampires in my game has a Technomage Fangirl. He's her Husbando; she has a technocratic paradigm and works out of a basement for the VAs. Her job? She looks at supernaturals and writes up reports on them. Using CCTV, local news, online messengers (and hacking) she finds Vampires, Werewolves etc. and writes up reports on them. If a VA (or allied Mages) need to know about the Anarchs in Manchester, she's got a file on them. And in the process of learning about this PC, she falls in love with him. Like her, he's emotionally distant. He's got an eyepatch and is very handsome. He's blank enough for her to project all of her tastes onto. She has a psychiatric report on him pinned to her wall, and she's put love hearts around the various neuroses he has, since they're similar to her own. Basically this led to her submitting a report which gave the Anarchs a lower threat level than she should have done, and she's been cleaning up after their digital footprint in her spare time. Players only know about this via &quot;cutscenes&quot;. Her powers? Technomancy 5, and some other powers (Auspex 2, Presence 4, Levinbolt 2) that are distinctly &quot;tech-based&quot;... so she can short-circuit a machine remotely, or scan an aura by running some CCTV footage through a special program, but she can't just conjure up lightning from thin air or see someone's aura with her eyes.<br /> <br /> Werewolves? Well besides their Healing Factor and their Forms, they get Disciplines. Theurgists get &quot;blood magic&quot; reskinned. I do this with every splat, and I keep the lore and themes which work and don't get too bulky. Wraiths are a thing, and have Fetters, but lack Shadows, as just one example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T07:16:43-07:00","id":1123476,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123353#post1123353\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, my post wasn't in response to you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> It was a general thread-topic thing.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> That said, my usual issue with Arete vs skillpool contested rolls is that you then require high-Arete Archmages to be able to contest even potential fresh-out-of-chargen splats that specialize in those skills. It's relatively easy to justify an 8-dice attribute+ability combo with even a potential specialization out of CG if it's a character's thing.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Here's the thing. I'm ok with other splats having the advantage of immediate actions. Mages have the advantage of taking extra time. No amount of extra time will give the vampire more dice. A mage can spend the time building up his &quot;Vampire hunting ritual&quot;. Mages have flexability while other splats generally have fast readily available simple powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-01T11:31:19-07:00","id":1123568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1122651-obfuscate-and-other-supernatural-hiding?p=1123476#post1123476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's the thing. I'm ok with other splats having the advantage of immediate actions. Mages have the advantage of taking extra time. No amount of extra time will give the vampire more dice. A mage can spend the time building up his &quot;Vampire hunting ritual&quot;. Mages have flexability while other splats generally have fast readily available simple powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite right, and I get the spirit of what you're trying to do. I agree..Vampires, Werewolves, etc....they are the instant-action splats. The always-ready-for-go-time creatures.<br /> <br /> But leaving Arete as-is for those rolls means Mages can't win any contested actions that involve magic as they will potentially always have a much smaller dice pool than the other for every round of contest, and are also the worst splat at counterspelling. It's kind of ironic, really, if you consider the nature of those two things.<br /> <br /> So it's kind of a dilemma, as while the theme of the other splats being more instant-action is perfect, the ironic flipside is one of Mages being the worst at magical defense without an almost paranoid lifestyle.<br /> <br /> I consider the <i>'Arete counts for twice the sucesses in contests and counters vs. splats'</i> to be a good balance - it evens those odds between the splats for basic things, yet while *still* allowing the other splats to toss out their whole pack of abilities near instantly.<br /> A vampire can pump their strength, have passive extra bonuses to dex, and toss out a dominate effect in the same round without any preparations - instant alpha strike, and without any tools, gadgets or practices needed - while this still remains very hard for a mage to do, not mentioning justification with a good RPed paradigm. They can go for Wonder creation (expensive) or Time 4 (needs preparation and paradigm again), and both take effort, investment and RP.<br /> <br /> And yes, I think a Mage's counterspelling needs paradigmatic action - it's not reflexive, IMO. If a Mage doesn't have their tools, or even if they have their tools but are lazing on a chair with the hands in their pockets, they have a hard time justifying a counterspelling action from my point of view. Another benefit of having managed to drop an instrument, but unless a lot of instruments are dropped, the array of instantly counterspellable things is narrow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":".  Typo fixings! 08-01-2017, 03:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}